---
title: "update_price_feeds_client (Pyth Sui Price Feeds: Use Real-Time Data)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_connect: connection = new SuiPriceServiceConnection(hermes_url, binary=true)
    q_connect --> q_fetch_offchain: priceUpdateData = connection.getPriceFeedsUpdateData(priceIDs)
    q_fetch_offchain --> q_init_client: pythClient = new SuiPythClient(suiClient, pythStateId, wormholeStateId)
    q_init_client --> q_build_tx: transaction = new Transaction()
    q_build_tx --> q_update_feeds: priceInfoObjectIds = pythClient.updatePriceFeeds(transaction, priceUpdateData, priceIDs)
    q_update_feeds --> q_validate_result: suiPriceObjectId = priceInfoObjectIds[0]
    q_validate_result --> q_error: suiPriceObjectId is undefined
    q_error --> [*]: throw Error("suiPriceObjectId is undefined")
    q_validate_result --> q_add_move_call: suiPriceObjectId is defined
    q_add_move_call --> q_set_gas: transaction.moveCall(target=oracle::get_sui_price, args=[CLOCK, suiPriceObjectId])
    q_set_gas --> q_sign: transaction.setGasBudget(1000000000)
    q_sign --> q_execute: result = suiClient.signAndExecuteTransaction(transaction, signer=keypair)
    q_execute --> [*]: return result

    note right of q_fetch_offchain
        INV-001: priceUpdateData must contain signed VAA from Hermes
        INV-002: binary=true required for on-chain verification
    end note

    note right of q_update_feeds
        INV-003: updatePriceFeeds adds pyth::update_single_price_feed call to transaction block
        INV-004: Price update must use the latest Pyth package version
    end note

    note right of q_validate_result
        INV-005: priceInfoObjectIds must contain at least one element per requested priceID
    end note

    note right of q_sign
        INV-006: keypair must have sufficient SUI for gas budget
    end note
